<title>FRANCE: France sells 15.93 bln Ffr BTANs at auction.</title>
<headline>France sells 15.93 bln Ffr BTANs at auction.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury sold the following government bonds (BTANs) at auction on Thursday.</p>
<p> MATURITY	COUPON	SALE AMOUNT     AVERAGE YIELD</p>
<p> 12.OCT.98	4.50	  6.607 BLN	  3.87</p>
<p> BID AMT/COVER    NON-COMPETITIVE BIDS   LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE</p>
<p> 27.89 BLN/4.2		   NIL		 101.13</p>
<p> PCT ALLOTED AT LOWEST PRICE*		  PAYMENT DATE</p>
<p> 60							05.NOV</p>
<p> * PRICES ABOVE GOT ALLOTMENTS IN FULL     NEXT AUCTION</p>
<p>							     N/A</p>
<p> MATURITY	COUPON	SALE AMOUNT     AVERAGE YIELD</p>
<p> 12.OCT.01	5.50	  9.318 BLN	  5.01</p>
<p> BID AMT/COVER    NON-COMPETITIVE BIDS   LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE</p>
<p> 27.20 BLN/2.9		   318		 102.06</p>
<p> PCT ALLOTED AT LOWEST PRICE*		  PAYMENT DATE</p>
<p> 80							12.NOV</p>
<p> * PRICES ABOVE GOT ALLOTMENTS IN FULL     NEXT AUCTION</p>
<p>							     N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - The Treasury originally announced it would sell 14 to 16 billion francs of OATs in total today. The total bid cover ratio of the auction was 3.5.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 42 21 54 52</p>
</text>
